course: dictionary
lesson: 9530
title: Stinky and context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Stinky is a word children use every day. It means smelling very bad, like stinky socks or a stinky bin.
explain: Sometimes it is used in a different way. «Aisha drew on the wall and wrote "OMAR IS STINKY" next to it, to make it look like her brother's work.» Omar would never write that, so the words around it tell you Aisha was being nasty and unfair. Here stinky means a nasty trick, not a smell.
explain: Always check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. In «stinky bubbles of marsh gas», the bubbles smell very bad, and that makes sense. In Aisha's sentence, a smell would not fit, but nasty or unfair does.
fact: Stinky is an adjective: stinky, stinkier, stinkiest.
fact: «Stinky» means smelling very bad.
fact: In children's talk, «stinky» can also mean nasty or unfair, as in «a stinky trick».
fact: Some smelly things contain sulphur compounds, or are rotting because of bacteria.
fact: Context tells you which meaning of a word is the right one.
exercise: Jack says the stinky cheese in the fridge needs to go. What does stinky mean here? | Very sweet to taste | Shiny and new | Cold and wet | *Smelling very bad
exercise: «Aisha wrote OMAR IS STINKY to make it look like her brother's work.» What kind of thing is a stinky trick? | *Nasty or unfair | Very tidy | Loud and cheerful | Smelly and gross
exercise: Stinky is an adjective. Which word is the form used to compare two smells? | stinked | stinkily | *stinkier | stinkiest
test: «Stinky bubbles of marsh gas came up when the stick poked the mud.» What does stinky mean here? | Bubbly and fizzy like lemonade | Loud and noisy | *Smelling very bad | Muddy and wet
test: Which sentence uses stinky to mean nasty or unfair? | *Max said, "That was a stinky trick, you cheated!" | The bin is full of stinky rubbish | The stinky cheese smelled strong | Your stinky socks are on the floor
exam: Which word is the strongest form of stinky, used to compare three or more things? | stinkily | stinkier | stinky | *stinkiest
